WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.610
It's Saturday, and this is the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.270
Here are the last 24 hours at Microsoft, in 3 minutes.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.090
Heads up, school IT: the next Windows Server drops WSUS,

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:21.580
the role that pushes out updates.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.180
Server 2025 and earlier keep it, supported for their whole lifecycle.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.270
Shared PCs in the lab? Windows Server 2028,

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:39.210
now in preview, also removes MultiPoint Services.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.200
Imaging PCs over the network?

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.300
Windows Deployment Services is deprecated there; plan your move.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:47.140
For coding classes,

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:51.830
Visual Studio's November update turns on the new Copilot Chat by default.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.430
Drag files straight into a prompt,

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:57.880
and steer Copilot mid-task without waiting for it to finish.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.200
Building a campus search or chatbot?

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.690
Azure AI Search can now follow your storage permissions.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.120
So people only see results from files they can already open.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:12.700
It's generally available.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.710
Campus servers on Windows Server 2025?

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:21.780
An extra hotpatch fixes a crash after November's update.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.360
It hits some servers using IPv6 router advertisements,

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.500
and the fix needs no restart.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.190
Something calmer: Microsoft 365's Calendar,

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:37.270
People and Files companion apps retire on December 16.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.820
Nothing's lost: your files, meetings and contacts stay put.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:44.530
Use Outlook, Teams or File Explorer.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.890
The fine print?

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:51.160
Researchers say a fake Snipping Tool download installed a malicious Microsoft Store app.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.390
And Edge's planned Copilot options to summarise,

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:58.460
translate and cite highlighted text are cancelled.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:07.420
After hours, Hela: of Mice & Magic lands on Game Pass on December 1.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:11.120
You're a brave little mouse,

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:15.230
helping others one kind act at a time, in split-screen co-op too.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:22.020
And Rayman Legends Retold, out December 3, brings four-player couch co-op.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:28.590
Plan the server move, check your downloads, then go play: that's your heads up.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.350
Zoom out, and it never stops shipping.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.340
Today's board: shipped. Tomorrow's: already building.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.970
That's one day of updates. Imagine a whole year.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.870
You've been watching the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.120
Same time tomorrow?
